WEBVTT

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:09.210
It'd be impossible to hide it now.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.400
Setting aside the particulars of 
the destruction of Chimidoro,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.120
since she transformed into a salamander 
in front of everyone, it can't be helped.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.360
Wow!

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.420
So she's a real vampire?

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.000
All right. I've found the 
heroine of my next film.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.190
I knew she was no ordinary girl.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:30.890
Yeah, you can't expect to 
request that for free.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.450
That's not what I meant!

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:35.280
Anyway, that's the situation.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.940
I'd like to ask everyone involved 
to please help us take care of Mai.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:42.880
Consider everyone here as 
that girl's guardians.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.350
No objections!

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.800
It's the only thing to do.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.300
You don't need to strain yourselves.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.860
Just a little help here and there is enough.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.570
Just a little?

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:56.060
How can you take such a careless approach 
when you're playing such an important role?

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:56.590
What?

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:57.960
Don't give me that crap!

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:01.340
Listen here. When a man protects a girl—

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.600
But I'm a girl, too.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:07.430
Rather, when a girl like you 
protects another girl...

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:09.100
In other words...

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.790
When you're protecting someone you love...

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.840
You have to be willing 
to risk your own life!

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.160
And all the blood in your body!

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.750
You must be prepared to defend 
her until the very end!

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.850
That's what he's trying to say!

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.610
That's right!

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:19.330
Osu!

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:22.580
Don't use the word "osu!"

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:22.590
<b>SLAP SLAP SLAP</b>

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:29.530
Since the sun is setting, let's continue 
this discussion without those four.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.050
In order to keep Mai under our supervision,

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:37.220
starting today, we'll enroll her 
in night classes at this school.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:38.860
Night classes?

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.250
Our school offers those?

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.760
Our school's doors are open to 
young working people, as well.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.410
I had no idea.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:46.150
Neither did I.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.400
Me, neither.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.910
To be precise, we've decided 
to open our doors.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.340
Decided to? Which means...

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:58.190
Starting today, Seijumonji High 
School will offer night classes.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.850
What?

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.470
You're out of your mind.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.200
<i>Is the doctor trying to 
keep Mai all to herself?</i>

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.540
Who's keeping her to themselves?

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.390
Don't worry.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:11.440
The night classes were officially 
authorized by the board of directors.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.490
You got their permission? How?

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.660
It's a long story.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:19.570
Could you try to keep it short?

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.940
Don't ask me for the details.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.580
To put it simply, here's what happened.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:29.120
By the way, from here on out, I'll be 
speaking in only Shin Hasegawa lines.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.340
Hasegawa?

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:31.970
He was a handsome film and stage actor

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:34.460
who appeared in films from 
the prewar to postwar period.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.680
Everyone knows that.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:37.740
That's Kazuo Hasegawa!

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:41.970
Why don't you read some books instead 
of watching movies all the time?

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.210
<b>SLAP SLAP SLAP</b>

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:45.470
<b>SLAP SLAP SLAP</b>

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:46.900
Shin Hasegawa is the playwright who created 
the Japanese movie genre Matatabi-mono!

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:44.970
<b>Matatabi-mono
(Wandering Gamblers)</b>

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.640
<b>SLAP SLAP SLAP</b>

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.050
<b>In Search of Mother</b>

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:50.230
He's famous for writing <i>In Search 
of Mother</i> and <i>Kutsukake Tokijiro</i>!

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.220
<b>SLAP SLAP SLAP</b>

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.180
<b>Kutsukake Tokijiro</b>

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.120
Could you summarize that for us?

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:55.700
Since it's a long story, 
I'll omit certain elements.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.700
In order to reach this point,

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:03.360
I risked my life and faced 
fires, floods, and winds.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:09.050
To be brief, I risked my life in numerous 
games of dice in order to get their permission.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:11.240
You don't need to explain whole process.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.000
Just give us the conclusion.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.600
I'm glad you asked, mister.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.260
To put it simply, here's what happened.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:19.540
I'm not a mister.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.780
Since it's a long story, 
I'll omit certain elements.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:25.330
In order to reach this point...

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.220
<b>- Chihiro's Flashback -</b>

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.220
<b>Censored</b>

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:37.930
And so, they authorized night classes.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.860
We live in a soft world.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.570
In other words, you used 
your sexual charms on them.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:46.710
Well, the world is only soft on sexy women.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:48.570
I learned something today.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:51.790
Anyway, I'll be swapping 
to night classes, too.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:52.970
So will I.

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:53.960
And me.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:55.310
Me, too.

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.610
What? You, too?

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.330
Of course.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.920
We're her guardians, too.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.200
We'll be joining you.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.470
Same as above!

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:05.170
It's the only thing to do.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:09.360
But I'd hate to trouble you guys.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.000
I appreciate the thought, though.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.350
I'm a man. A warrior never 
goes back on his word.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:15.500
Who's a warrior?

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.890
By the way,

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:20.110
anyone enrolled in 
night classes will automatically

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:22.430
be signed up for the Blood Donation Club.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:23.630
No objections!

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:24.360
Objection!

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.720
No boys are allowed in the Blood 
Donation Club. It's for girls only.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.490
Where and when...

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:30.600
And who decided that?

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.820
Was it Yukio Aoshima at the National Diet?

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.860
Who's Yukio Aoshima?

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:35.830
I dunno.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:39.420
Haven't you heard of the 
Equal Employment Opportunity Law?

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.810
"Sudara Bushi?" "Granny Mischief?"

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:42.790
No clue.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.900
School Regulation Article 32.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.710
He was in "Bubble Holiday," too...

00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:54.760
Except during natural catastrophes 
and other emergency situations,

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.490
loud shouting, angry yelling, and coquettish 
shrieking are prohibited within the school.

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:01.040
<i>Great, another freak showed up.</i>

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:03.980
Doctor, I'd like to enroll 
in night classes, too.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:04.570
What?

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:08.550
There's no way night classes would be 
conducted properly with these students.

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:12.860
For the sake of Seijumonji High School's 
honor, I must offer my assistance, as well.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:16.100
<i>She's just bored, too.</i>

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.800
Jinko, what's your blood type?

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:21.680
Type A. What about it?

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:25.410
Based on her upright and steadfast personality, 
you should've known that without asking.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:28.870
Didn't you previously reject 
that as popular belief?

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:30.050
Of course.

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:34.020
Determining a person's personality based 
on blood type has no scientific basis.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.030
What are you two chattering about?

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.640
Is there something wrong with being type A?

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:40.970
<i>All right. Now we have 
girls of all blood types.</i>

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:49.400
Jinko

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:49.400
Maki

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:49.400
Kaoru

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:49.400
Nami

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:47.200
Just so you know, I'm only enrolling in 
night classes so I can maintain discipline.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.380
I have no intention of getting 
involved in your foolish nonsense.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:53.780
Chimera

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:53.780
Mitsugu

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:52.050
<i>What a stubborn girl.</i>

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:53.580
Who's stubborn?!

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.190
Mitsugu, everyone can hear your thoughts.

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:58.780
We can hear everything.

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:04.570
As the only night class teacher and advisor 
to the Blood Donation Club, I'll arbitrate.

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:05.500
Mitsugu Bambam.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:06.220
Bamba!

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:07.450
Maki Watabe.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:08.650
Nami Unten.

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:09.750
Kaoru Konno.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:11.410
Jinko Sumida.

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:15.900
I grant you permission to enroll in night 
classes and join the Blood Donation Club.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:20.210
Doctor Chihiro, I'd like to decline 
joining the Blood Donation Club.

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.730
<i>What a stubborn girl.</i>

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.490
Who's stubborn?!

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:26.770
I'll allow Masumi Katsuno and 
the others to enroll in classes,

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.770
but you'll be joining the 
Blood Donation Club as backups.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:31.820
You'll be our strategic reserve 
in case the other four dry up.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:35.530
We're doing this for the continued 
existence of humanity and world peace.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:38.720
All of us must protect Mai's secret.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:41.830
You mustn't give Mai any 
blood without my permission.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:45.700
Naturally, letting Mai suck your 
blood directly is inexcusable.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.090
Roger!

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:51.690
<i>For the continued existence 
of humanity and world peace.</i>

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:54.460
<i>I know what I said,</i>

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:59.040
<i>but it kind of feels like Mai 
is drifting away from me.</i>

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:13.840
<i>But it's true that there's only so much 
I can do on my own to protect Mai.</i>

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:20.010
That's near my house.

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:23.290
There's a lot of bats out today.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:24.290
<b>This Side Up</b>

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.290
<b>Keep Dry</b>

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:29.790
<b>Perishable</b>

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:31.520
What is this?

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.170
Who sent us this huge thing?

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:36.380
Wait a minute. This size...

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:37.500
Could it be?

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.640
Yikes. I knew it.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:52.600
But who would pull a prank like this?

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:06.000
Hello.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.690
I am Mai's father Gillesde Rais.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:11.670
<b>Gillesde Rais</b>

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:11.660
What? Mai's dad?

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.180
I heard you've been taking 
care of my daughter.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:16.510
Thank you, thank you.

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:19.760
Daddy.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.800
Ah, Mai. Have you been a good girl?

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:26.690
Daddy, hurry up and divorce that old bitch.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:29.320
Didn't we promise not to talk about that?

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:32.820
That horrible ugly bitch is deceiving you.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:36.270
There, there. You want a Chanel bag, is it?

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:39.520
If you don't divorce her, 
I'll become a delinquent.

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:43.560
I see, I see. You want a Prada bag.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:46.420
Should I make some tea?

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:48.690
Oh, no need to be so considerate.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:51.450
I'm terribly sorry for making 
you worry about dinner.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.840
Why don't we go out to eat?

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:55.110
What?

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:02.080
This place makes delicious gyoza.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:10.140
<b><b>Gyoza General</b></b>

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:06.080
I see. Then perhaps I'll have an 
extra large helping of those.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:08.690
Are you okay with garlic?

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:10.140
I love garlic.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.770
But Mai experiences side effects.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:18.000
Mai has had food allergies 
since she was a child.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:21.110
I thought she'd gotten over them.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:23.620
It's because I'm experiencing 
psychological stress.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.130
They've gotten worse since 
that old bitch showed up.

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.270
You promised to call her "Mommy."

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:29.960
I never promised that.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.160
I'm going to go to the bathroom.

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:35.170
Who's more important, me or that old bitch?

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.350
At least call her Rebeus.

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:40.920
Then who's more important, 
me or Rebeus the hag?

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:44.380
You'll see once you get here.

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:47.700
It's an opportunity to see a super rare dad.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.950
If you don't hurry, you'll regret 
it for the rest of your life.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:52.350
Here's your extra large order of garlic 
gyoza with extra garlic

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:55.850
and extra large garlic fried 
rice with extra garlic.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:00.310
I haven't had gyoza 
this good in 120 years.

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:02.510
After all, they're free.

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:05.810
I feel like having garlic fried rice today.

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:09.640
Would you like me to order 
another plate for you?

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:12.150
Please, there's really no 
need to be so considerate.

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:15.810
One extra large garlic yakisoba and 
one extra large garlic fried rice!

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:19.500
One extra large garlic yakisoba and one 
extra large garlic fried rice. Got it.

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:23.160
Six garlic spring rolls 
and six garlic shumai!

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:26.360
That's six garlic spring 
rolls and six garlic shumai.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:28.670
What? You want to get some to go, too?

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:29.890
If you insist.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:33.180
Three giga-large orders 
of garlic yakisoba to go!

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:36.820
Three giga-large orders 
of garlic yakisoba to go.

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:37.690
He's still ordering.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.440
By the way, since Mai 
will be staying with you,

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:42.960
as her father, I'd like 
to ask you something.

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:44.630
Yes?

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.660
What's your blood glucose level?

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:51.780
I believe it's around 82 
milligrams per deciliter.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:55.650
I think those are normal levels.

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:58.620
What about your red blood cell, 
white blood cell, and platelet levels?

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:01.160
I believe they're all normal.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:03.100
That won't do.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:07.990
If you're going to be living with Mai, 
you need to know your precise values.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:09.580
Yes, sir.

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:11.910
What about your family?

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:14.080
My dad's currently overseas.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:16.830
Overseas? What does he do?

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:19.410
He's a scholar.

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:20.690
A scholar.

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:23.770
Where does he teach?

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:27.640
He teaches archaeology at the 
Royal Danish University of Helsink.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.880
University of Helsink? Archaeology?

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:34.910
Thanks for waiting.

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:39.380
You came. Doctor Chihiro, 
that took you long enough.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:41.170
Doctor?

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:44.620
This is Doctor Chihiro, 
my high school's doctor.

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:48.690
Nice to meet you. 
My name is Chihiro Chimatsuri.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.850
What a beautiful woman!

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:53.880
Hello.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:56.070
I am Mai's—

00:13:56.070 --> 00:13:59.650
